// The engine's reading of a `pick_at` node: the adjoint of the read, `[0.0, 1.0, 0.0]`.
//
// `grad` is `autodiff:grad`, whose reverse pass asks `DerivativeRegistry` for a rule filed under the
// node's operator (`modules/autodiff/pullback.cpp`, "no derivative rule for operator"). The read the
// engine knew under its own spelling is `:op/idx_arr` (`src/builtin/operators/derivative.cpp`), which
// is what `xs[i]` is; `pick_at` is the second spelling of the same read with the length stated
// (`modules/tensor/ops/layout_ops.cpp#elementAtKernel`). This program is the one whose reading was
// once a refusal, and it is now the reading of the number.
//
// ---- settled: which entry, and when ----
//
// `lane-pickat` answered the read in the library and left the engine's side filed as an account
// rather than a wall: `jvp` gave the tangent `0.25`, `vjp` gave the gradient `[0.0, 1.0, 0.0]`, and
// the two closed on the direction (`pick_at_forward_rule.cml`), while this program stopped at
// `autodiff: no derivative rule for operator 'tensor:pick_at' of type 'float'` -- a missing row in
// the engine's C++ table, not a missing law. The pin that recorded it named its own settlement: the
// day someone filed a `setVjp` for `pick_at`, this file was to be turned into the positive reading
// of the same program, `engine dL/dw=[0.0, 1.0, 0.0]`, the number the library's `vjp` answers.
//
// `lane-pickatvjp` filed that row (2026-11-04) -- `setVjp(defs, "pick_at", &pickAtVjp)` at the end of
// `layoutOps` in `modules/tensor/ops/layout_ops.cpp`, beside the `take` and `idx_take` entries -- and
// flipped this file with it. The rule is the read's own adjoint: zeros in the differentiated
// tensor's shape with the cotangent added at `at[0]` (`pickAtVjp`), the construction the core files
// for `:op/idx_arr`, so the two legs of the account are one number now:
//
//     engine dL/dw=[0.0, 1.0, 0.0]
//
// The library's leg of the same read prints the same array in `pick_at_forward_rule.cml`.
//
//     camel test/cases/compile/transforms/pick_at_gradient_answered_by_the_engine.cml
import { grad } from autodiff
import { pick_at } from tensor

/// The differentiated value is the `with` parameter (design principles 9.9).
with <w: float[]>
func read(): float {
    return pick_at(w, [1, 3])
}

func main(): int sync {
    let slope = grad(read)
    let d = slope<[1.0, 2.0, 3.0] as float[]>()
    `engine dL/dw={}`->format<d>->println
    return 0
}